273
00:11:17,463 --> 00:11:19,880
So the basic idea is we're
learning the input to the query

274
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:22,301
and keeping the key
value input the same.

275
00:11:22,301 --> 00:11:24,700
The downside or the
sort of upside of this

276
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:28,660
is that when we compute the
attention map after this, now

277
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:30,970
we basically turned this
from a square matrix

278
00:11:30,970 --> 00:11:34,060
to a rectangular matrix--

279
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:37,030
and reduces the complexity
of the matrix multiplied

280
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:40,240
to O of MN, so now it's
linear in the input size.

281
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:44,240
And the second matrix multiply
has the exact same property.

282
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:47,500
So it from quadratic,
it becomes linear.

283
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:49,690
And the quite cool
thing about this

284
00:11:49,690 --> 00:11:51,340
is that, OK, so
the cross-attention

285
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:54,525
