457
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:40,920

458
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:43,140
At a high level, this
gives us an architecture

459
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:44,400
that we can apply to images.

460
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,690
But it doesn't make
any assumptions

461
00:18:45,690 --> 00:18:46,680
about image structure.

462
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,900
So it's one that you
can use elsewhere.

463
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:54,700
And we basically, we give
information about the input

464
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:58,110
sort of spatial structure by
having positional coatings

465
00:18:58,110 --> 00:19:01,110
and here we use a 2D Fourier
