470
00:19:14,490 --> 00:19:17,070
So this is basically a
Fourier decomposition

471
00:19:17,070 --> 00:19:19,710
of the position of the 2D input.

472
00:19:19,710 --> 00:19:23,520
And a couple of things that we
found with that, if we sampled

473
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:25,680
the frequency, that's the
maximum frequency that's

474
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:28,440
used up to the Nyquist
frequency of the signal,

475
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:31,050
we end up doing
better than if you

476
00:19:31,050 --> 00:19:32,423
use a lower version of this.

477
00:19:32,423 --> 00:19:33,840
And this basically
